ing":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the concrete subphase-instrumentation mechanism (which seams: shared interpreter vs. aggregating the recorder's existing per-step duration_ms by op-name in gate_dispatch.py) and state a positive rationale for the choice, explicitly weighing the recorder-aggregation alternative that avoids editing the shared workflow engine.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["gate_dispatch.py:763-773 measures verifier_workflow_ms as one interval around _ex.run_workflow(...)","interpreter.py:489 records _t_step per leaf and _run_batch:408 per batch, all persisted via step records carrying step_id/kind/duration_ms","gate_dispatch.py:648-664 _sum_run_consumption already walks rec.steps summing duration_ms by kind (agent vs other)","gate_dispatch.py:789-791 verifier_workflow_step_count already computed from len(recorder.steps)","tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py:488-501 shows run_workflow populating recorder.steps with per-step kind+duration_ms as the established data shape","ABSENCE: the plan states no positive rationale for its chosen decomposition mechanism and does not identify which seams ('existing seams only' is unresolved between the shared interpreter and the local recorder-aggregation path)"],"finding":"The plan does not name WHERE the new subphase seams live, and a structurally-different, lower-blast-radius alternative appears at least as good but is not weighed. verifier_workflow_ms wraps a single run_workflow call in gate_dispatch.produce_completion_verdict; the precheck/verify/reconcile ops it must attribute run inside the shared interpreter (_execute_frame) that also serves the plan-review and code-review gates. The interpreter ALREADY records per-step kind+duration_ms, and _sum_run_consumption in this same file already aggregates rec.steps to compute llm_ms/det_ms while verifier_workflow_step_count is derived from len(recorder.steps). Aggregating those recorded per-step durations by op-name inside gate_dispatch.py would decompose workflow_ms while touching only the local dispatcher (not the shared engine consumed by all three gates), reusing an existing data source, and remaining trivially testable with synthetic recorder.steps (the existing test already exercises exactly this shape). The plan's 'monotonic duration measurements at existing seams only' does not disambiguate between instrumenting the shared interpreter vs. this recorder-aggregation path.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"febb1cfa7e5b5bcd4","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan section 'Plan' bullets 1-2 ('Trace the completion workflow call path and define concrete, non-overlapping subphase boundaries...' / 'Add monotonic duration measurements at existing seams only'); AC line 1","norm_id":"n9eca15fae19bcafd","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer instruments the shared interpreter/executor to attribute the completion workflow, changing timing behavior for the plan-review and code-review gates that share the engine","Reviewer/author cannot tell whether the residual will absorb genuine interpreter orchestration cost or hide a mis-placed seam"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Prefer deriving the precheck/verify/reconcile subphase durations by summing the recorder's already-captured per-step duration_ms (grouped by step_id/op-name) inside produce_completion_verdict, an